Bug 2083485 - Don't give calendar server credentials to an HTTP proxy in cal.auth.Prompt. r=tobyp

cal.auth.Prompt took the origin from channel.URI. On a proxy challenge
that URI is still the calendar server, so the server's saved password
went to the proxy without asking.

Refuse challenges flagged AUTH_PROXY. Proxies that ask for Basic or
Digest credentials can't be used for calendars until proper proxy auth
is added. NTLM and Negotiate proxies are answered by necko with the
system credentials and are not affected.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337947


diff --git a/calendar/base/modules/utils/calAuthUtils.sys.mjs b/calendar/base/modules/utils/calAuthUtils.sys.mjs
--- a/calendar/base/modules/utils/calAuthUtils.sys.mjs
